 that is not confirmed the  other thing is the guardians of the  galaxy vol 3 trailer is mostly finished  when they showed it at san diego  comic-con the cgi and graphics weren't  all done but it does appear like they  have the scenes that they want to put in  the trailer all edited out now this  isn't really likely if we are going to  get a trailer it's most likely going to  be for ant-man and of course some disney  plus shows however having said that i  think there is some footage that could  be shown at d23 like footage for the  marvels we know they have footage of the  film and at sdcc they showed us footage  of guardians 3 and ant-man and the wasp  quantomania and the marvels as the next  film to come out so there is always the  possibility that they could tease us  with footage from the marvels after all  they do need to tease footage at d23 it  is separate than sdcc so they still have  to tease things and make people really  excited and although if they do this it  won't be released to the public of  course people who are attending d23 are  able to describe what they saw so we'll  have a good description of what the  trailer is like now to get into a little  bit more exciting things like blade we  don't know much about blade right now we  just know mahershala ali is going to be  playing blade but i'm expecting him to  come on stage with kevin feige and i'm  expecting them to give us a little bit  of info about blade maybe our first look  at him in the actual outfit and maybe  even announce who the villain could  possibly be or at least the cast this is  a big one for marvel studios so i'm  expecting a little bit of time at least  focused on blade in fact i'm expecting a  little bit of time for the last six  projects of phase five i think they're  going to kind of divide their time i  think half of it is going to be spent  talking about phase five and half of it  is going to be spent revealing phase six  so that first half talking about phase  five i think mos